    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109482" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόφαυσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>narrow opening,</i> in the bridge across the Hellespont,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.36
			</span></i>; in a testudo, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				99.39
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ θυρίδες δικτυωταί, ὑποφαύσεις
					κύκλῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ez.</u>
					41.16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφαύσιας</span> was read for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφάσιας</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				2
			</span></i> by Artemidorus and Dioscurides ap.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).52
			</span></i>, but rejected by <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> l. c.</div>
